  'Pin-up · The flood lot · 5:30 PM':'方案展示 · 被淹的空地 · 下午5:30','Dry {0} in 10':'10次里{0}次不淹','Tinker some more':'再调一调','Next: night orders':'下一步：夜间命令',
  'How do you present it?':'你打算怎么介绍它？',
  'Here’s the {0}. In a big storm, the street should stay dry about {1} times in 10, not every time. {2} What do you think?':'这是{0}。遇到大暴雨，10次里街道大约有{1}次不会被淹，不是每次都不淹。{2}你们觉得怎么样？',
  'There’s no shade yet.':'现在还没有遮阴。','It has shade for hot afternoons.':'下午热的时候有遮阴。',
  'It’s perfect. This lot will never flood again, I promise, and everybody gets what they asked for.':'它太完美了。这块地再也不会被淹，我保证，每个人想要的都能得到。',
  'Trust me, this is the right design for all of you. You don’t need to worry about the details.':'相信我，这个设计对你们每个人都合适。细节你们不用操心。',
  'Seven feet! Okay, now we’re talking.':'七英尺！好，这才像话。',
  'Four feet is kind of a baby bowl. But it’s a start.':'四英尺有点像小朋友玩的碗池。不过总算开了个头。',
  'That bowl is so gentle, my little cousin could skate it.':'那个碗池也太平缓了，我小表弟都能滑。',
  'A skate path around a garden? It’s... curvy. I guess.':'绕着花园的滑板道？挺……弯的吧，大概。',
  'A plaza and a little bowl? I’ll take it!':'有广场，还有个小碗池？我要了！',
  'A flat plaza is fine for tricks, but there’s no bowl.':'平广场练招式是可以，可是没有碗池。',
  'Rails and ledges! It’s not a bowl, but it’s fun.':'有栏杆还有台面！虽然不是碗池，但挺好玩。',
  'There’s nothing here to skate at all.':'这里根本没东西可以滑。',
  'There’s shade, a bench with a back, and a ramp for my walker. Now I can sit near it.':'有遮阴，有带靠背的长椅，还有我推助行架能走的坡道。这下我能坐在旁边了。',
  'Steps? With my walker? I’ll be watching from my kitchen.':'台阶？我推着助行架怎么上？那我只能在厨房里看了。',
  'Lovely. But with no shade, I’ll cook on that bench by ten in the morning.':'挺好看。可是没有遮阴，上午十点我坐在那张长椅上就要被烤熟了。',
  'I’m not giving my face to a gate just to sit on a bench.':'就为了坐个长椅，还要把我的脸交给一道门？我不干。',
  'And where exactly do I sit?':'那我到底坐哪儿？',
  'The street stays dry in about nine big storms out of ten? I can work with those odds.':'十场大暴雨里大约有九场街道不被淹？这个把握我能接受。',
  'That’s better than now, but some big storms would still flood my street.':'比现在好，可有些大暴雨还是会淹到我这条街。',
  'That won’t keep my twenty-three homes dry.':'这样保不住那二十三户人家不被淹。',
  'And it’s over the 400-coin budget. The city won’t pay that.':'而且超出了400金币的预算，市里不会出这个钱。',
  'Never? Like, never ever?':'永远不会？真的永远永远不会？',
  'Nobody can promise that. The weather decides how big a storm gets.':'谁也保证不了。暴雨有多大，是老天说了算。',
  'Can we at least see the bowl?':'至少让我们看看碗池吧？',
  'I’m the one who signs for the drains, so I need to see the numbers.':'排水是我签字负责的，我得看到数字。',

